  Author: Rafael M. Koike & Cursor Agent ("Ada")

  Hardened-runtime entitlements. The two JIT allowances are not optional for Electron: V8
  generates code at runtime, and without them a *notarized* build crashes on launch while the
  unsigned local build works perfectly — which is the most misleading failure in the whole
  packaging path, because nothing about it points at entitlements.

  `allow-dyld-environment-variables` is what lets the Electron framework load its own dylibs
  under a hardened runtime.
-->
<plist version="1.0">
  <dict>
    <key>com.apple.security.cs.allow-jit</key>
    <true/>
    <key>com.apple.security.cs.allow-unsigned-executable-memory</key>
    <true/>
    <key>com.apple.security.cs.allow-dyld-environment-variables</key>
    <true/>
  </dict>
</plist>
